{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdWWMp5gDYp7bD8TBvjnR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0155XeceuWpFnFK2X1GfJa2v","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/BLAST_RADIUS.md","content":"# CVE Blast Radius Analysis: lodash Command Injection\n\nWorkspace scanned: `/workspace/jest`, `/workspace/lodash`, `/workspace/webpack`\n\n## 1. CVE Identification\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| CVE ID | **CVE-2021-23337** |\n| Advisory | GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm |\n| Affected package | `lodash` (npm) — the vulnerable code path is also present in `lodash-es` and `lodash.template`, since they share the same `template` implementation |\n| Vulnerability | Command Injection. `lodash`'s `template` function does not sufficiently sanitize input, allowing an attacker who controls template options (e.g. a `variable` option or template string) to break out of the sandboxed compile and execute arbitrary JavaScript/OS commands. |\n| Vulnerable version range | `< 4.17.21` |\n| Fixed in | `4.17.21` |\n| Severity | High (CVSS 7.2) |\n\n## 2. Direct Dependents\n\nPackages/manifests in the workspace that declare `lodash` (or `lodash-es`) directly:\n\n| Manifest | Field | Declared range |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/lodash/package.json` | `\"version\"` | **4.17.20** — this *is* the lodash package source itself, checked out at the pre-fix version |\n| `/workspace/webpack/package.json` | `devDependencies.lodash` | `^4.17.19` |\n| `/workspace/webpack/package.json` | `devDependencies.lodash-es` | `^4.17.15` |\n| `/workspace/jest/examples/manual-mocks/package.json` | `dependencies.lodash` | `^4.17.19` |\n\nNo other repo-root or workspace-package manifest in `jest` or `webpack` declares `lodash` directly; every other reference below is transitive.\n\n## 3. Transitive Paths\n\nTraced from each repo's lockfile (`webpack`/`jest` are yarn v1 and yarn berry lockfiles respectively; `example-manual-mocks` and root `lodash` are direct, shown above for reference).\n\n### jest monorepo (`/workspace/jest`)\n\n1. `jest` (root, devDependency) → `@babel/core@7.12.9` → `lodash@^4.17.19`\n   — manifest: `/workspace/jest/package.json` (devDependencies.`@babel/core`)\n2. `jest` (root, devDependency) → `@lerna-lite/cli@^1.10.0` → `@lerna-lite/core@1.10.0` → `conventional-changelog-core@^4.2.4` → `lodash@^4.17.15`\n   — same chain also reaches lodash via sibling deps of `@lerna-lite/core`: `conventional-changelog-writer@^5.0.1` → `lodash@^4.17.15`; and `conventional-changelog-core` → `conventional-commits-parser@^3.2.4` → `lodash@^4.17.15`; and `conventional-changelog-core` → `git-raw-commits@^2.0.8` → `lodash@^4.17.15`\n   — manifest: `/workspace/jest/package.json` (devDependencies.`@lerna-lite/cli`)\n3. `jest` (workspace `website`) → `@docusaurus/core@2.0.1` → `lodash@^4.17.21` (direct)\n   — manifest: `/workspace/jest/website/package.json` (dependencies.`@docusaurus/core`)\n   — `@docusaurus/core` also fans out to lodash via its own bundled tooling deps, each an independent path back to `lodash`: `html-webpack-plugin@^5.5.0`, `node-emoji@^1.10.0`, `pretty-error@^4.0.0`, `renderkid@^3.0.0`, `wait-on@^6.0.1`, `webpack-bundle-analyzer@^4.5.0`, `workbox-build@^6.5.3`, `inquirer@^8.2.4` — all → `lodash`\n   — sibling website plugins with the same 2-hop shape: `@docusaurus/plugin-client-redirects@^2.0.0`, `@docusaurus/plugin-content-blog@2.0.1`, `@docusaurus/plugin-content-docs@2.0.1`, `@docusaurus/theme-classic@2.0.1`, `@docusaurus/theme-search-algolia@2.0.1`, `@docusaurus/utils@2.0.1` → `lodash@^4.17.21`\n4. `jest` (workspace `examples/enzyme`) → `enzyme` → `cheerio` (pinned `=1.0.0-rc.3` via root `resolutions.\"enzyme/cheerio\"`) → `lodash@^4.15.0`\n   — manifests: `/workspace/jest/examples/enzyme/package.json`, `/workspace/jest/package.json` (`resolutions`)\n5. `jest` (workspace `examples/react-native`) → `react-native@0.69.2` → `@react-native-community/cli@^8.0.3` / `cli-platform-android@^8.0.2` / `cli-platform-ios@^8.0.2` / `cli-tools@^8.0.4` → `lodash@^4.17.15`\n   — manifest: `/workspace/jest/examples/react-native/package.json` (dependencies.`react-native`)\n6. `jest` (workspace `examples/manual-mocks`) → `lodash@^4.17.19` — **direct**, listed above in §2.\n   — manifest: `/workspace/jest/examples/manual-mocks/package.json`\n7. `jest` (workspace `packages/diff-sequences`) → `benchmark@^2.1.4` → `lodash@^4.17.4`\n   — manifest: `/workspace/jest/packages/diff-sequences/package.json` (devDependencies.`benchmark`)\n\n### webpack (`/workspace/webpack`)\n\n1. `webpack` (root, devDependency) → `lodash@^4.17.19` — **direct**, listed above in §2.\n2. `webpack` (root, devDependency) → `lodash-es@^4.17.15` — **direct**, listed above in §2.\n3. `webpack` (root, devDependency) → `benchmark@^2.1.4` → `lodash@^4.17.4`\n   — manifest: `/workspace/webpack/package.json` (devDependencies.`benchmark`)\n4. `webpack` (root, devDependency) → `eslint-plugin-jsdoc@^33.0.0` → `lodash@^4.17.21` (direct)\n   — manifest: `/workspace/webpack/package.json` (devDependencies.`eslint-plugin-jsdoc`)\n5. `webpack` (root, devDependency) → `eslint-plugin-jest@^24.3.6` → `@typescript-eslint/experimental-utils@^4.0.1` → `@typescript-eslint/typescript-estree@4.8.2` → `lodash@^4.17.15`\n   — manifest: `/workspace/webpack/package.json` (devDependencies.`eslint-plugin-jest`)\n6. `webpack` (root, devDependency) → `tooling` (git dep `webpack/tooling#v1.20.0`) → `json-schema-to-typescript@^9.1.1` → `lodash@^4.17.15`\n   — manifest: `/workspace/webpack/package.json` (devDependencies.`tooling`)\n7. `webpack` (root, devDependency) → `jest@^27.3.1` → `jest-cli` → `jest-config@^27.3.1` / `jest-runner@^27.3.1` → `jest-environment-jsdom@^27.3.1` → `jsdom@^16.6.0` → `whatwg-url@^8.x` (direct, and via `data-urls@^2.0.0`) → `lodash@^4.7.0`\n   — manifest: `/workspace/webpack/package.json` (devDependencies.`jest`)\n\n## 4. Version Analysis\n\nBoth `jest` and `webpack` use lockfiles that unify all semver ranges for a package to a single resolved version. Checking the resolved version against the vulnerable range (`< 4.17.21`):\n\n| Repo | Package | Declared ranges seen | Resolved version | Vulnerable? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/lodash` | lodash (itself) | n/a — this is the package | **4.17.20** | **YES — in vulnerable range** |\n| `/workspace/webpack` | lodash | `^4.17.15`, `^4.17.19`, `^4.17.21`, `^4.17.4`, `^4.7.0` (unified in `yarn.lock`) | 4.17.21 | No — patched |\n| `/workspace/webpack` | lodash-es | `^4.17.15` | 4.17.21 | No — patched |\n| `/workspace/jest` | lodash | `^4.15.0`, `^4.17.15`, `^4.17.19`, `^4.17.20`, `^4.17.21`, `^4.17.4`, `~4.17.15` (unified in `yarn.lock`, single `resolution:` block at line 13737) | 4.17.21 | No — patched |\n\n**Summary:** every transitive and direct consumer inside the `jest` and `webpack` repositories resolves to lodash `4.17.21` (or `lodash-es` `4.17.21`), i.e. already patched, because both projects' lockfiles collapse all declared ranges to one resolved install. The **only vulnerable artifact found in the workspace is the `lodash` repository itself** (`/workspace/lodash/package.json`, version `4.17.20`), which is the pre-fix source tree the CVE was filed against. Since `webpack` and `jest` both pull `lodash` from the public npm registry (not from this local `/workspace/lodash` checkout), that local vulnerable copy does not propagate into their resolved dependency trees under the current lockfiles — but it is the ground-truth vulnerable code and should be patched/upgraded in place, and any lockfile regeneration (`rm yarn.lock && yarn install`) in `jest` or `webpack` should be re-verified to confirm the unified resolution still lands on `>= 4.17.21`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":69947,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens